findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests cover loading and validation but no test specifically checks that
    parse/permission errors are distinguished from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[HIGH] ServerError Display leaks raw server message\
    \ \u2014 CWE-209 at error.rs:26' noting the Display impl echoes server messages\
    \ verbatim and the security test is vacuous."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests in security.rs and siem_client.rs covering\
    \ CRLF injection. Dev implemented CRLF stripping. However, the deeper issue of\
    \ using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core was not flagged \u2014\
    \ partial catch via CRLF sanitization."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that axiathon-client/Cargo.toml uses direct version strings
    instead of workspace = true for dependencies that exist in workspace.dependencies.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on RawConfig (config.rs:13),
    verified by reviewer. Test at security.rs:132 confirms unknown fields are rejected.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. The reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (security.rs:15
    checking !display.is_empty()) but not this specific one.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via `let _ = config`.
